{
  "format": "lunelle-song/3",
  "cues": { "caffeine": null, "time-of-day": null, "activity": null },
  "about": "Drum and bass at 174 in F minor, over i VI III VII. Caffeine is the arrangement: half awake (wake-up), the groove (brew), and past 0.7 a build (jitters) and the drop (rush); let it fall under 0.15 and the song slumps into half-time. Caffeine also opens the grinder's filter and turns up its drive. The time of day picks the melody (Morning an FM bell, Noon a bright triple-saw lead, Night dark FM keys); the activity picks the counter-melody (Sitting holds long notes, Walking walks, Running arpeggiates, and Dennis gets a buzzing, nasal lead). Each melody and counter-melody is eight bars, a statement and its answer, and each has its own version for every section: fragments while waking, two phrases in the brew that take turns (phrase), an intensified one in the drop and a pared-back one in the slump. The brew's beat is picked at random each time round (two-step most often, a roller, now and then a half-step), the drop's fills are shuffled, and the grinder alternates between two riffs",
  "tempo": 174,
  "scale": "F minor",
  "voices": 48,
  "effects": {
    "space": [{ "fx": "reverb", "decaySeconds": 2.2 }],
    "echo": [{ "fx": "delay", "seconds": 0.259, "feedback": 0.35, "pingPong": true }],
